// Each rule below is one way the JSON `rule` can match.
// Columns after `at` are the metavariables the JSON's message, anchor or `each` names: one finding per distinct row.
// The JSON `transform` computes KN from other metavariables' text; its literals end each rule.
.violation C416_set_comprehension(at: node, c416_comp: node, it: loc) code "C416" "Replace this comprehension with `set({it})`, which copies the same items; keep it inside `__len__`, where `set()` can recurse."
    suppress noqa "C416"
C416_set_comprehension(COMP, n, IT) :- node(_, n, _, _, _), W = n, c416_alt_19(n, COMP, IT, KN, _, _),
    text(W, t1), KN = @replace_all(t1, "(?s)^.*$", "set").

